 \, the president of the Confederacy\, was captured when the Union Army cau
 ght up to him on May 10\, 1865\, in Irwinville\, Georgia. He would spend 2
  years in prison before being released without going to trial.</p>\n<p></p
 >\n<p></p>\n<p>Brought to you by <a href='http://americanhistorycalendar.c
 om'>http://AmericanHistoryCalendar.com</a>.<br/>\nLike our Facebook page t
 o see upcoming history events in your feed <a href='https://www.facebook.c
 om/AmericanHistoryCalendar/'>https://www.facebook.com/AmericanHistoryCalen
 dar/</a>.</p></body></html>
DESCRIPTION:Jefferson Davis\, the president of the Confederacy\, was captur
 ed when the Union Army caught up to him on May 10\, 1865\, in Irwinville\,
  Georgia. He would spend 2 years in prison before being released without g
 oing to trial.\n\n\nBrought to you by http://AmericanHistoryCalendar.com.
 \nLike our Facebook page to see upcoming history events in your feed https
 ://www.facebook.com/AmericanHistoryCalendar/.
